I agree that the you kill monster 1-monster 2 steps up to monster 1's
square-monster 2 picks up the nasty item you barely survived last time-
monster 2 nails you with said nasty item has gotten VERY old.

If (and I do mean if) it makes sense to allow most monsters to use most
items, then they MUST be required to move, pickup, and use on separate
turns--just like us.  This is a MAJOR problem in some situations.

Speaking of monster use of items, does it make sense for monsters to
randomly zap wands?  This running down of necessary resources is VERY
rough.  I don't think monsters should be able to use wands of digging,
either--sections of the dungeon can get cut off.  Not to mention having
to retame your pet all the time.

Does anyone know why your pet no longer recognizes you if it changes levels?
This seems like a bug to me.


